   "evidence": "Norm.lean: `| k + 1, ... => eLpNorm f p (volume.restrict U) + \u2a05 D (_ : HasWeakFDerivOn volume (Opens.interior U) f D), eLpNormWkp p U k D`. Weak differentiability on an empty open set is vacuous, so D = 0 is admissible and the infimum is 0. Roadmap \u00a73.2: `\u2016\u03be\u2016_{W^{k+1,q}(K)} \u2264 C(\u2016\u2202\u0304\u03be\u2016_{W^{k,q}(\u03a9')} + \u2016\u03be\u2016_{Lq(\u03a9')})` for compact K.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Complex/Wirtinger/Regularity.lean",
   "fix": "Measure the derivatives over K itself. Either (a) also return an open `\u03a9''` with `K \u2286 \u03a9''` and bound `eLpNormWkp p \u03a9'' (k+1) u`, or (b) state the bound with the L\u1d56(K) norms of the iterated weak derivatives taken on \u03a9, as the first-order `exists_eLpNorm_le_of_hasWeakConjWirtingerDerivOn_of_le` already does.",
   "issue": "`exists_eLpNormWkp_le_of_hasWeakConjWirtingerDerivOn` bounds `eLpNormWkp p K (k+1) u` for an arbitrary compact `K`. That norm takes the infimum over weak derivatives on `interior K` only, so `D` can be zero on `K \\ interior K`. For a fat-Cantor-type `K` (empty interior, positive measure) the left side is just `\u2016u\u2016_{L\u1d56(K)}` and no derivative is controlled. The roadmap's `\u2016\u03be\u2016_{W^{k+1,q}(K)}` measures the derivatives over all of K.",
